The file-level source/variant mapping is `cleanup/slot2-8f-ref-artifact-map-2026-10-05.tsv`. For a path shared by branch revisions, the map records every exact source blob and the selected version. The selected report files are newest by last path-touch time among these source tips; current `main` paths were not overwritten.

## Preserved families

- Adjacent O-O cusp, strip, switching, and three-cut reductions.
- High-t paired-remainder, ladder, phase-zero, and terminal-free grid reductions.
- Collapsed support-six regressions and constrained chamber candidates.
- Earlier C-II exact-phase, flat-center, gluing, inactive-wall, and penetration/hidden-rank discovery reports from this hash shard.

The marker-rectangle and cusp-multiregion source refs share the same final report blobs; the TSV records both source tips against the selected files. The old §§155-156 pure-tooth module is not copied into `docs/targets`; PR #392 records that its exact regression and metric incidence result are superseded by audited §§158-159 on main. The earlier all-phase harmonic-concentration target module is retained only as `research/legacy_target_modules/...`, outside the active route.

## Verification limits

This archival import does not claim that each source theorem is valid. The already adopted #692/#693/#697 verifiers passed from their exact PR snapshots; the Slot 2 adjacent/high-t/support-six selected checks are listed in #635. One support-six metric exploration timed out at 120 seconds and is not used to support a theorem claim. Most imported historical verifier scripts are preserved but were not re-run in this cleanup.
